WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.805 --> 00:00:34.830
So really importantly in this case is to discuss with this young woman what her

2
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:40.560
current symptoms are and the timing of what is her known underlying rhinitis.

3
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:46.231
Now, in this patient, who's very specific of knowing she has mild rhinitis or hay

4
00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:52.020
fever during the spring pollen season, well, this is early winter, so we don't

5
00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:57.030
expect this to be the same cause. And this should highlight the practitioner to

6
00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:00.660
curiously wonder if this is maybe rhinitis of pregnancy.

7
00:01:08.235 --> 00:01:13.665
Now, rhinitis of pregnancy is under the subclass of non-allergic rhinitis, and it

8
00:01:13.711 --> 00:01:19.170
is hormonally influenced and very common in roughly 20% of pregnant women in the

9
00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:22.470
second trimester, and it typically resolves after birth.

10
00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:28.590
Now, the important features of rhinitis of pregnancy is this congestion, and also

11
00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:33.961
that it may be managed with non-pharmacological treatment like isotonic or

12
00:01:33.975 --> 00:01:39.195
hypertonic intranasal saline, which will make the woman happy because she's not

13
00:01:39.211 --> 00:01:43.665
using pharmaceuticals, and it might also alleviate her symptoms.

14
00:01:43.711 --> 00:01:49.410
So isotonic nasal saline is equivalent to our body's normal salt concentration, and

15
00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:53.521
this helps, of course, improve the mucociliary clearance, decreasing congestion,

16
00:01:53.641 --> 00:01:57.976
and sort of ridding the nose of any allergens or pollutants that might be around,

17
00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:01.349
as well as helping with the hormonal congestion.

18
00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:06.915
But if it can be tolerated, hypertonic saline can help even further.

19
00:02:06.961 --> 00:02:11.955
And this is because it has a slightly saltier concentration than our body, and this

20
00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:17.715
will create an osmotic drive from the mucosal tissue into the nasal passages,

21
00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:20.535
thereby clearing some of that congestion even further.

22
00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:26.940
So you can reassure that both of these, whether isotonic or hypertonic saline, are

23
00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:32.296
safe to use in pregnancy and are non-pharmacological and well-tolerated.

24
00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:44.160
When a pregnant woman has rhinitis of pregnancy, and this could be mixed with their

25
00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:48.870
underlying allergic rhinitis or on its own, it's really important to stress to the

26
00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:53.910
patient that it is okay to trial non-pharmaceutical treatments like intranasal

27
00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:58.050
saline, either isotonic or hypertonic, in the first instance.

28
00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:02.655
Now, if this doesn't work, we have to have another conversation about the risks and

29
00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:06.660
benefits of what their residual symptoms are and whether that needs to be treated

30
00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:10.171
with more pharmaceutical management like a third-generation intranasal

31
00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:16.171
corticosteroid or an oral antihistamine to see if maybe their management

32
00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:20.671
could be helped further. And this, of course, needs to be taken into consideration

33
00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:24.360
with their antenatal care provider, their GP, and the patient.
